d, 11's record is gone in the step 12 was observed, and no\n1094:  alternates signed 11 and 13 at every poll, and the mesh answers no\n1116:- **A malformed index.** A signed, verified trace naming a hash-valid\n1132:  `:no-key`, each appending nothing.\n1150:and its status line, which says \"design target\" of code that exists\n1153:an owner question; no fallback is designed, because none is expected.\n1171:- **A shared key.** Two serving nodes with one key answer two\n1190:- `dht join <token>` passes no `--dht-manifest` and saves\n1194:  `--dht-manifest` with a saved follow suspends following for that run.\n1207:  joins with the token and requires it on each of the four VMs, on the\n1215:Each of the first four is its own later design; section 8.2 says what\n1219:- **Relaying.** Decided as a deferral: no node re-serves a head in the\n1229:  against `dao.stream.md`, outside this design. Its fix is to resolve\n1237:- **Collecting superseded indexes; key rotation; a head history; a\n1242:1. **Does \"always\" reach into a live session?** The design keeps a\n1245:   running session, relink in place needs its own design first. No\n1247:2. **What should a bare `q` see after `dht join`?** Already ruled: the\n1249:   Open: the default. Today join hydrates, so a bare `q` answers the\n1250:   publisher's facts. Here join does not, so it answers the reader's own\n1261:   design follows it; it was said before this cost was stated. The\n1268:   NATs would need a relay pair, or the deferred UDP design. It is\n1274:   cleartext channel a path attacker can alternate old signed heads so\n1290:the Architect's and the independent reviewer's sign-off on the contract\n1294:the return-path proof, are deferred with their designs; publisher\n1306:relay rings, `--dht-recover`, the removal of hydration, and slice H5.\n1311:would then need a redesign. The document was rewritten, not patched,\n1317:   candidate slot and no eviction. The latest observed trace takes it,\n1322:   newer trace is observed and the newer load starts at once;\n1334:   recorded for the deferred design.** No UDP mirror is built. Section\n1336:   stated requirement of that later design, with `dao.stream.udp` and\n1340:the one-slot rule and resolved. A wrong or unloadable signed trace can\n1356:- **N8. Revision 1 removed hydration to fix D1 and then had to add\n1358:  that join used it. Revision 2 stops join using it and touches nothing\n1377:   key is the alias again. Revision 2's note N5 read the landed\n1403:276, and 8.2 says what the reserved `ws:<port>` does not cover.\n1415:signed value on a ring one agent writes and any agent may read, carried\n104:    \"--dht-max-inbound-bytes\" \"--dht-manifest\" \"--dht-key\" \"--dht-principal\"\n167:(defn load-key\n178:      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-key \" path \": the key file does not exist; \"\n180:                           \"--dht-keygen \" path \")\")\n184:      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-key \" path \": the key file is refused (\"\n207:                 (ex-info (str \"--dht-keygen \" path \": the file exists; \"\n237:                        (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-keygen \" path \": \"\n244:   (`--dht-keygen`), and answer the lines to print and the exit status.\n395:      [\"--dht-keygen\" (or file (state-path (or name \"publisher\") \".key\"))])))\n404:   `[args {:new-key path}]`.\"\n433:           key (into [\"--dht-key\" key])\n443:         {:new-key (when (= \"init\" verb) key)\n447:          ;; --dht-key must not survive `serve` or `join` (a --key named on\n449:          :unset (when-not (= \"init\" verb) #{\"--dht-publish\" \"--dht-key\"})}]))))\n474:   the arguments say beyond flags: `:new-key` (a key file `init` makes),\n511:   evaluation; `--dht-key file`, the publisher's stable key file\n517:   without `dht:<dir>` is refused.  `--dht-keygen file` writes a new key\n565:          \"--dht-key\" (recur (nnext args)\n566:                             (assoc opts :dht-key-file\n569:                                                 \"--dht-key needs a key file\"\n579:          \"--dht-keygen\" (recur (nnext args)\n580:                                (assoc opts :dht-keygen\n583:                                                    \"--dht-keygen needs a file\"\n604:                              :dht-key (:dht-key opts)\n708:   \"values, and the result is saved. --dht-manifest and --dht-keygen are\"\n711:   \"dht flags (need --index-store dht:<dir>, except --dht-keygen):\"\n719:   \"  --dht-key file              the publisher's key file\"\n723:   \"  --dht-keygen file           write a new key file and exit\"\n775:   `--dht-keygen` composes nothing: it writes the key file and answers\n777:   `--dht-key` file is loaded here (`load-key`); the key reaches the\n786:             [args {:keys [new-key unset] node-name :name dir :dir}]\n789:                                 (not (some #{\"--dht-keygen\"} args)))\n795:             resolved (state/resolve-flags saved flags unset)\n797:             made (when (and new-key (nil? (fs/read-file-text\n798:                                             (first (split-path new-key))\n799:                                             (second (split-path new-key)))))\n800:                    (:lines (keygen! new-key)))\n814:         (if-some [path (:dht-keygen opts)]\n816:           (let [key (some-> (:dht-key-file opts) load-key)\n822:                                     :dht-key key\n897:                 (:publisher opts) \" (key from \" (:dht-key-file opts) \")\"))\n899:      (conj (str \"dht: no --dht-key: (yin.link/publish ...) is refused; names\"\n904:  \"Print a composition that ends at startup -- `--dht-keygen` -- and end\n                     (.prompt rl))\n                 ;; Headless has no reader, so the explicit stop trigger is the\n                 ;; host\n                 ;; signal: it appends a line, nudges, and returns, like any\n                 ;; producer.\n                 (doseq [signal [\"SIGINT\" \"SIGTERM\"]]\n                   (.on js/process signal (fn []\n                                            (request-stop! state\n                                                           w))))))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; cljd: a stdin listener that only appends, and one periodic timer owner\n;; =============================================================================\n\n#?(:cljd\n   (do\n     (defn- write-line!\n       [message]\n       (println message))\n\n     (defn- print-prompt!\n       []\n       (.write io/stdout prompt)\n       (.flush io/stdout))\n\n     (defn- run-dart!\n       \"One wake source owns the tick: exactly one `Timer` armed per round, at\n        the interval `cadence-step` computes over `default-cadence`, because a\n        synchronous poll loop would deadlock the Dart event loop: IO never\n        progresses, so `blocked` never clears.  Returns the wake so the\n        composition can wire its line producers (the stdin listener, the\n        stop signals) as `nudge!` callers.\n\n        `:stopping` is nil while the shell runs and a tick budget afterwards:\n        the endpoint is asked to stop once and stepped at the base interval\n        (a bounded drain, not a curve) until it reports it, so the host does\n        not exit with a live listener.\"\n       [state server headless?]\n       (let [box (atom {:state state :server server :stopping nil\n                        :cadence (cadence/init default-cadence)})\n             wake-ref (volatile! nil)\n             finish! (fn []\n                       (wake/disarm! @wake-ref)\n                       (close-index-store! (:state @box))\n                       (io/exit (exit-status (:state @box)))\n                       nil)\n             tick (fn []\n                    ;; The periodic timer this namespace replaced fired\n                    ;; again whatever happened, so a tick whose body throws\n                    ;; must not kill the owner: arm the fallback first and\n                    ;; let the body's own `arm!` replace it. `finish!`\n                    ;; disarms, so a finished owner parks nothing.\n                    (wake/arm! @wake-ref tick-millis)\n                    (let [{:keys [state server stopping cadence]} @box\n                          now (.-millisecondsSinceEpoch\n                                (dart-core/DateTime.now))]\n                      (if (nil? stopping)\n                        (let [[state' server' lines]\n                              (step-all state server now)]\n                          (reset! box {:state state'\n                                       :server server'\n                                       :stopping nil\n                                       :cadence cadence})\n                          (doseq [line lines]\n                            (write-line! line))\n                          (cond\n                            (:running? state')\n                            (let [{:keys [cadence-state sleep-ms]}\n                                  (cadence/cadence-step\n                                    cadence (moved? state' server' lines))]\n                              (swap! box assoc :cadence cadence-state)\n                              (when (and (seq lines) (not headless?))\n                                (print-prompt!))\n                              (wake/arm! @wake-ref sleep-ms))\n\n                            server'\n                            (do (swap! box assoc\n                                       :server (serve/stop! server')\n                                       :stopping stop-ticks)\n                                (wake/arm! @wake-ref tick-millis)\n                                nil)\n\n                            :else (finish!)))\n                        (let [[server' lines stopped?] (stop-tick server now)]\n                          (doseq [line lines]\n                            (write-line! line))\n                          (cond\n                            stopped? (finish!)\n                            (zero? stopping) (do (write-line! stop-timeout-text)\n                                                 (finish!))\n                            :else (do (swap! box assoc\n                                             :server server'\n                                             :stopping (dec stopping))\n                                      (wake/arm! @wake-ref tick-millis)\n                                      nil))))))]\n         (vreset! wake-ref (wake/make-wake tick))\n         (wake/arm! @wake-ref tick-millis)\n         @wake-ref))\n\n     (defn -main\n       [& args]\n       (let [started (startup args {:persist? true})]\n         (when (contains? started :exit) (exit-with! started))\n         (if-some [refusal (:refusal started)]\n           (refuse! refusal)\n           (let [{:keys [opts state server]} started\n                 headless? (boolean (:headless? opts))]\n             (doseq [line (banner opts)]\n               (write-line! line))\n             ;; The tick owner arms its first round, and the composition wires\n             ;; the\n             ;; deposit it hands each line producer with the nudge: a typed line\n             ;; ends the idle sleep at once.  A timer fires only on the event\n             ;; loop, so arming before the producers are wired races nothing.\n             (let [w (run-dart! state server headless?)]\n               (if headless?\n                 ;; Headless has no reader, so the explicit stop trigger is the\n                 ;; host signal: it appends a line, nudges, and returns, like\n                 ;; any\n                 ;; producer.\n                 (-> (.watch io/ProcessSignal.sigint)\n                     (.listen (fn [_signal] (request-stop! state w))))\n                 (do (-> io/stdin\n                         (.transform (.-decoder convert/utf8))\n                         (.transform (convert/LineSplitter.))\n                         (.listen (fn [line]\n                                    (driver/submit-line! (:input state) line)\n                                    (wake/nudge! w))\n                                  .onDone (fn []\n                                            (driver/submit-line! (:input state)\n                                                                 \"(quit)\")\n                                            (wake/nudge! w))))\n                     (print-prompt!))))))))\n\n     (defn ^{:dart/name main} run-main\n       [args]\n       (apply -main args))))\n    80\t  evaluator chosen at the prompt with `(vm :type)` is not saved; start with\n    81\t  `--vm` to save one.\n    82\t- **Changing it:** a flag overrides the saved value for that setting, and the\n    83\t  result is saved. A repeated flag (`--dht-peer`, `--dht-principal`,\n    84\t  `--dht-follow`) replaces all of its saved values rather than adding to them.\n    85\t  `dht init` saves publishing and a key; `dht serve` and `dht join` clear both\n    86\t  from the saved state (a `--key` on that command line still stands). A bare\n    87\t  switch\n    88\t  `--reset`.\n    89\t- **`--reset`** forgets the saved state and starts from the command line\n    90\t  alone; the result is saved. **`--no-state`** neither reads nor writes it,\n    91\t  for a one-off run.\n    92\t- **Refusals:** a state file that cannot be read, or saved flags that clash\n    93\t  with the command line (saved `--dht-*` flags with `--index-store mem`), refuse\n    94\t  startup, naming the file and `--reset`. A state file that cannot be written\n    95\t  is a warning, and the node still starts.\n    96\t- **Hosts:** ClojureDart has no home directory, so a bare `yin-repl` there\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
